   PROGRAM CURSES.PROBE
* udt_curses — CALLC.EXISTS and CURSES.AVAIL, against a cfuncdef we control.
* Copyright (C) 2026 Gordon Heydon.  GPL-2.0-only.
*
* Run it in an account with the two functions cataloged:
*
*   UniData   BASIC BP CURSES.PROBE ; RUN BP CURSES.PROBE
*
* It prints FAILURES=0 when both are right.
*
* WHY IT WRITES $UDTHOME/bin/work/cfuncdef.  CALLC.EXISTS is DEFINED as "is
* this name in UniData's canonical CallC definition file".  It reads that path
* and nothing else, because a live probe is impossible -- a CallC to an
* unregistered function aborts the whole program, which is the reason the
* function exists.  So testing it means controlling that file.
*
* THE FIXTURE IS WRITTEN FROM SCRATCH, NOT APPENDED TO.  A host that already
* has CURSINIT registered would make the "absent" cases pass or fail for
* reasons that have nothing to do with the code under test.  Every case below
* is asserted against a file this program just wrote, and the original is put
* back at the end.
*
* BOTH DIRECTIONS, ALWAYS.  A probe stuck on one answer is the failure mode:
* answer 0 for everything and every caller silently takes the fallback path
* for ever; answer 1 for everything and callers CallC into a function that is
* not there, which aborts them.  Neither shows up in a test that only asks
* about a name it expects one answer for.
   DEFFUN CALLC.EXISTS(A)
   DEFFUN CURSES.AVAIL(A)
   FAILS = 0
   NL = CHAR(10)
*
   UDT = GETENV("UDTHOME")
   IF UDT = "" THEN
      PRINT "UDTHOME is not set -- there is no cfuncdef to control, not passing"
      PRINT "FAILURES=1"
      STOP
   END
   CFD = UDT : "/bin/work/cfuncdef"
   OSREAD ORIG FROM CFD ELSE ORIG = ""
*
* A minimal well-formed cfuncdef: the three section markers install.sh writes,
* and no functions between them.
   BASE = "$$FUN" : NL : "$$OBJ" : NL : "$$LIB" : NL
   PROBE = "$$FUN" : NL : "ZZPROBEFN:string:1:string" : NL : "$$OBJ" : NL : "$$LIB" : NL
   CURSED = "$$FUN" : NL : "CURSINIT:string:1:string" : NL : "$$OBJ" : NL : "$$LIB" : NL
*
* CAN WE WRITE IT AT ALL?  Everything below rests on that, and a test that
* cannot lay its own fixture has measured nothing -- so say so and fail,
* rather than reporting whatever the host happened to contain.
   OSWRITE BASE ON CFD
   OSREAD CHK FROM CFD ELSE CHK = ""
   IF CHK # BASE THEN
      PRINT "cannot write " : CFD : " -- no fixture, so nothing below is a test"
      PRINT "FAILURES=1"
      STOP
   END
*
   OK = (CALLC.EXISTS("ZZPROBEFN") = 0)
   IF NOT(OK) THEN FAILS += 1
   PRINT "1 absent name is not found    ok=" : OK
*
   OSWRITE PROBE ON CFD
   OK = (CALLC.EXISTS("ZZPROBEFN") = 1)
   IF NOT(OK) THEN FAILS += 1
   PRINT "2 registered name is found    ok=" : OK
*
* Re-reads the file rather than answering from the first call.  Without this
* case, 1 and 2 would both pass on a function that cached its first answer.
   OSWRITE BASE ON CFD
   OK = (CALLC.EXISTS("ZZPROBEFN") = 0)
   IF NOT(OK) THEN FAILS += 1
   PRINT "3 gone again after rewrite    ok=" : OK
*
* An exact match on the name, not a prefix: CURS must not match CURSINIT, or
* every CURS* probe would answer for every other one.
   OSWRITE CURSED ON CFD
   OK = (CALLC.EXISTS("CURS") = 0)
   IF NOT(OK) THEN FAILS += 1
   PRINT "4 a prefix is not a match     ok=" : OK
*
   OK = (CURSES.AVAIL("") = 1)
   IF NOT(OK) THEN FAILS += 1
   PRINT "5 AVAIL sees CURSINIT         ok=" : OK
*
   OSWRITE BASE ON CFD
   OK = (CURSES.AVAIL("") = 0)
   IF NOT(OK) THEN FAILS += 1
   PRINT "6 AVAIL says no without it    ok=" : OK
*
* Put the host back as it was.  If there was no cfuncdef to begin with this
* leaves an empty one, which is what a UniData with no CallC contributions
* has anyway.
   OSWRITE ORIG ON CFD
   PRINT "FAILURES=" : FAILS
